2026-10-08T06:12:03.3340385Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3348633Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3424890Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3433232Z [0m
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3433622Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3434025Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3434343Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3434488Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3434982Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3435212Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3435425Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3435881Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3436035Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3436409Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3436871Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3437259Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3437558Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3437698Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3437893Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438217Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438363Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438570Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438646Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438712Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3438799Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3439013Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3440272Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3443282Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3443367Z I will:
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3443700Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3443970Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3444213Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3444460Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3444677Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3444828Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3444989Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3445399Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3445847Z    /root
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3456725Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3457170Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3469897Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3470356Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3470576Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3470813Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3471134Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3481960Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3482571Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3490518Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3491002Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3491383Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3491548Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3491703Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3491888Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3492106Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3492469Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3492640Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3492734Z If you would like to
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3492980Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3493136Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3493311Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3493636Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-08T06:12:03.3493765Z 
